            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I am not entirely sure what you mean here.\r\n\r\nThere are [suggested mappings for `<Tab>` and `<S-Tab>` in help file](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/07ad48937204446ba350837a3413a5d19de22c36/doc/mini-completion.txt#L96-L97). With them and default `config.set_vim_settings` (which sets `completeopt` option), you can press `<Tab>` while popup suggestions are visible which will lead to first suggestion placed in text. After that, you can continue typing text as usual. This is how I use it.\r\n\r\nIf you also want for dismiss popup after `<Tab>`, try this mapping (adds `<C-y>` in case of visible popup):\r\n```lua\r\nvim.api.nvim_set_keymap('i', '<Tab>', [[pumvisible() ? \"\\<C-n>\\<C-y>\" : \"\\<Tab>\"]], { noremap = true, expr = true })\r\n```\r\n\r\n... or a more modern approach:\r\n```lua\r\nvim.keymap.set('i', '<Tab>', [[pumvisible() ? \"\\<C-n>\\<C-y>\" : \"\\<Tab>\"]], { expr = true })\r\n```\r\n\r\nDoes this solve your issue?",
